{"name":"Sword Steel","hex":"#d6d2de","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sword","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long bladed weapon with a grip and typically a pommel and crossguard (together forming a hilt), which is designed to cut, stab, slash and/or hack.","A suit in certain playing card decks, particularly those used in Spain and Italy, or those used for divination.\nA card of this suit."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To stab or cut with a sword"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sword"},{"term":"steel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An artificial metal produced from iron, harder and more elastic than elemental iron; used figuratively as a symbol of hardness.","Any item made of this metal, particularly including:\nBladed or pointed weapons, as swords, javelins, daggers."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of steel.","Similar to steel in color, strength, or the like; steely."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sword","blocks":[{"text":"A sword is an edged, bladed weapon intended for manual cutting or thrusting. Its blade, longer than that of a knife or dagger, is attached to a hilt and can be straight or curved. A thrusting sword tends to have a straighter blade with a pointed tip. A slashing sword is more likely to be curved and to have a sharpened cutting edge on one or both sides of the blade. Many swords are designed for both thrusting and slashing. The precise definition of a sword varies by historical epoch and geographic region."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sword","wikidata":"Q12791"},{"title":"Steel","blocks":[{"text":"Steel is an alloy of iron and carbon that demonstrates improved mechanical properties compared to the pure form of iron. Due to its high elastic modulus, yield strength, fracture strength and low raw material cost, steel is one of the most commonly manufactured materials in the world. Steel is used in structures, in bridges, infrastructure, tools, ships, trains, cars, bicycles, machines, electrical appliances, furniture, and weapons."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/%D0%90%D1%80%D0%BC%D0%B0%D1%82%D1%83%D1%80%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B9_%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BA%D0%B0%D1%82.jpg/330px-%D0%90%D1%80%D0%BC%D0%B0%D1%82%D1%83%D1%80%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B9_%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BA%D0%B0%D1%82.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steel","wikidata":"Q11427"},{"title":"Steel blue","blocks":[{"text":"Steel blue is a shade of blue color that resembles blue steel, i.e., steel which has been subjected to bluing for protection from rust. It is one of the less vibrant shades of blue, and is usually identified as a blue-gray color. An archaic term for it is chalybeous."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Niter_and_Color_Case.jpg/330px-Niter_and_Color_Case.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steel_blue","wikidata":"Q1003676"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Espadon-Morges.jpg/330px-Espadon-Morges.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Espadon-Morges.jpg/330px-Espadon-Morges.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Swiss longsword, 15th or 16th century","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEspadon-Morges.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Western_Han_Iron_Sword.jpg/500px-Western_Han_Iron_Sword.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Western_Han_Iron_Sword.jpg/1280px-Western_Han_Iron_Sword.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Western_Han_Iron_Sword.jpg/500px-Western_Han_Iron_Sword.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Western Han iron sword","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWestern_Han_Iron_Sword.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Apa_Schwerter.jpg/500px-Apa_Schwerter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Apa_Schwerter.jpg/500px-Apa_Schwerter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Apa-type swords, 17th-century BC","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AApa_Schwerter.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Nebra_Schwerter.jpg/500px-Nebra_Schwerter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Nebra_Schwerter.jpg/500px-Nebra_Schwerter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The swords found together with the Nebra sky disk, c. 1600 BC","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANebra_Schwerter.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Hallstatt_%27C%27_Swords_in_Wels_Museum%2C_Upper_Austria.jpg/500px-Hallstatt_%27C%27_Swords_in_Wels_Museum%2C_Upper_Austria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Hallstatt_%27C%27_Swords_in_Wels_Museum%2C_Upper_Austria.jpg/1280px-Hallstatt_%27C%27_Swords_in_Wels_Museum%2C_Upper_Austria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Hallstatt_%27C%27_Swords_in_Wels_Museum%2C_Upper_Austria.jpg/500px-Hallstatt_%27C%27_Swords_in_Wels_Museum%2C_Upper_Austria.jpg?utm_